		{"id":"cf807797c6984371","type":"text","text":"# Verifiable Biology\n\n## DNA\n- [Trust Everything, Everywhere](https://www.aria.org.uk/opportunity-spaces/trust-everything-everywhere)\n- [\\[1904.05528\\] Review on DNA Cryptography](https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.05528)\n- [An Introduction to Protein Cryptography](https://eprint.iacr.org/2025/089)\n- [\\[2307.09322\\] A New Hybrid Cryptosystem Involving DNA,Rabin, One Time Pad and Fiestel](https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.09322)\n- [Intelligent Design in Action: DNA Cryptography \\| Science and Culture Today](https://scienceandculture.com/2025/02/intelligent-design-in-action-dna-cryptography/)\n- [SecureDNA: Free, Secure DNA Synthesis Screening Platform](https://securedna.org/)\n- [\"Genomic Sequence Encryption (GSE): a DNA-based cryptography scheme in living cells!\"](https://x.com/VerenaVolf/status/1725559100979978713)\n- [FHE-enabled DNA](https://x.com/furkanakalcom/status/1892523791462343081)\n- [pathogen detection](https://x.com/Simon__Grimm/status/1955293512951284023)\n\t- [Scaling Pathogen Detection with Metagenomics \\| IFP](https://ifp.org/scaling-pathogen-detection-with-metagenomics/)\n- [Unclonable Polymers and Their Cryptographic Applications](https://eprint.iacr.org/2022/658)\n- [Building Unclonable Cryptography: A Tale of Two No-cloning Paradigms](https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/702)\n- Unclonable cryptography\n- [Cryptography in the DNA of living cells enabled by multi-site base editing \\| bioRxiv](https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2023.11.15.567131v1)\n- [cryptography Search Results \\| bioRxiv](https://www.biorxiv.org/search/cryptography)\n- [Hidden Messages in DNA Could Reduce Biosecurity Risks \\| The Scientist](https://www.the-scientist.com/improving-ngs-efficiency-with-better-cfdna-library-prep-72827)\n- [Protein design meets biosecurity \\| Science](https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.ado1671)\n- [Is That DNA Dangerous? - Asimov Press](https://www.asimov.press/p/dna-screening)\n- [How Much Information is in DNA? - by dynomight](https://www.asimov.press/p/dna-information)\n- [A Protein Printer - by Asimov Press and Adaptyv Bio](https://www.asimov.press/p/machine)\n- [Privacy in the Genomic Era \\| ACM Computing Surveys](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/2767007)\n- [Hackers are turning DNA sequencing into a biosecurity nightmare - The Brighter Side of News](https://www.thebrighterside.news/post/hackers-are-turning-dna-sequencing-into-a-biosecurity-nightmare/)\n- \n## Neuroscience\n- [Eight Reasons to Prioritize Brain-Computer Interface Cybersecurity – Communications of the ACM](https://cacm.acm.org/research/eight-reasons-to-prioritize-brain-computer-interface-cybersecurity/)\n  \n## Chemistry/Material Science","x":810,"y":450,"width":970,"height":583},
